WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.501
-You guys, today is Friday,
and that's usually when I

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:03.567
catch up on personal stuff.

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:05.300
I check my inbox.
I return some emails.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.567
And I, of course,
send out thank you notes.

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:09.434
I'm was just running
a bit behind.

00:00:09.434 --> 00:00:10.868
I thought if you guys
wouldn't mind,

00:00:10.868 --> 00:00:12.234
can I write out my weekly
thank you notes

00:00:12.234 --> 00:00:13.267
right now for you guys?

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:14.400
Thank you.
I appreciate it.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:19.734
James, can I get some thank you
note writing music, please?

00:00:19.734 --> 00:00:22.567
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.567 --> 00:00:24.868
That's my dude right there.

00:00:24.868 --> 00:00:29.934
♪♪

00:00:29.934 --> 00:00:34.100
Thank you, bobsledding, for
being competitive Uber pooling.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:37.434
Get in, get in.

00:00:37.434 --> 00:00:38.734
-Two-man luge.

00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:41.167
-Nice to meet you.
-Double luge.

00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:42.567
♪♪

00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:45.501
-Thank you, curling,
for being the only sport

00:00:45.501 --> 00:00:47.634
in the world where world
class athletes can train

00:00:47.634 --> 00:00:49.234
by Swiffering their kitchen.

00:00:49.234 --> 00:00:52.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:52.901 --> 00:00:54.000
-Come on.

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:58.100
When's J. Lo coming out?
-What's that?

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.234 --> 00:01:00.300
-When's J. Lo coming out?
-Soon.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:01.400
We've got to do this bit, yeah.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:02.868
-You gotta do this bit first?
Okay.

00:01:02.868 --> 00:01:05.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:08.200
-Thank you, ski jumping,
for being the flying

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:09.968
squirrel of Olympic sports.

00:01:09.968 --> 00:01:12.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:12.834 --> 00:01:14.501
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:17.767 --> 00:01:21.367
-Thank you, free style skiers,
for being so good at skiing

00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:23.334
that you look like
you're bad at skiing.

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:25.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:25.701 --> 00:01:27.234
-Yeah!

00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:28.501
Hey!

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:30.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.367
-Thank you,
cross country skiing,

00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:36.901
or as I like to call you,
complicated walking.

00:01:36.901 --> 00:01:39.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:48.334
Thank you,
new Olympic sport monobob,

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:52.133
for not going by your more
accurate title, batmobiling.

00:01:52.133 --> 00:01:53.701
That would be cool.
[ Applause ]

00:01:53.701 --> 00:01:55.133
-Monobob?

00:01:58.334 --> 00:02:00.667
-Thank you,
passing the Olympic torch,

00:02:00.667 --> 00:02:02.200
for basically being
the world's largest,

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:03.934
"Hey, you got a light?"

00:02:03.934 --> 00:02:05.634
There you guys have it.
Those are the "Thank You Notes."

